  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/586b8a8d-d060-44fb-b06e-7166195168eb.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.24653in;height:1.94653in\" /></p><p>From the figure,</p><p>for the small circle, the radius is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;units and the centre is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Therefore,&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is the diameter of the circle,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>k</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p>",
